# PROJECT: BEAMPAIR
## Secure Browser-Based Remote Support and Device Inspection Platform

Act as a senior full-stack engineer, WebRTC specialist, Firebase architect, security engineer, and UI/UX designer.

Build a complete, production-oriented web application named **BeamPair**. The application allows an authorized administrator to pair with Android phones through QR codes and conduct explicitly authorized remote-support sessions using browser-supported camera, microphone, and screen-sharing capabilities.

Do not build merely a static UI or a demonstration dashboard. Implement the actual application architecture, authentication, database operations, secure pairing, signaling, media connections, session management, error handling, and testing wherever the required services and credentials are available.

If a service requires configuration or credentials, create the necessary integration points and clearly document the setup. Never pretend that an unconfigured service or unimplemented feature is working.

