# 30. DEFINITION OF DONE

The application is not complete merely because the dashboard looks attractive.

The initial release must have:

- Working Google authentication.
- Enforced administrator authorization.
- Secure pairing-token generation and redemption.
- Functional QR pairing.
- Real device registration.
- Protected Firestore access.
- Real-time session signaling.
- WebRTC camera and microphone streaming where supported.
- Screen sharing where supported and explicitly approved.
- Device revocation.
- Session history.
- Security audit logging.
- Connection diagnostics.
- Proper resource cleanup.
- Meaningful error messages.
- Documented deployment instructions.
- No fake success states.
- No hardcoded mock data presented as live information.
- No unsupported claims about Android browser capabilities.

Features that cannot be implemented in an ordinary Android webpage must be identified clearly instead of being simulated.

